      "title": "Search query built from request input",
      "description": "Search puts the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Nothing escapes or binds the value. Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL. An injected query can read or change any data the database user can reach. Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Remove the Sprintf call.",
      "suggested_change": "\trows, err := h.DB.QueryContext(r.Context(), \"SELECT id, name FROM users WHERE name = ?\", name)",
      "source": "semgrep:go.lang.security.injection.tainted-sql-string.tainted-sql-string",
      "candidate": "c1",
      "notes": [],
      "problem": "Search puts the name query parameter straight into the SQL text with Sprintf. Nothing escapes or binds the value.",
      "consequence": "Any caller of GET /users can inject SQL. An injected query can read or change any data the database user can reach.",
      "fix": "Pass name to QueryContext as a bound parameter. Remove the Sprintf call."
    },
    {
      "origin": "agent",
